# Evidence manifest

Selected headline claims in the README (not every number in it), each traced to the saved file it comes from. Generated by `scripts/evidence_manifest.py`, which re-reads each artifact, formats each number the way the README states it and compares the two. Evaluation types are kept apart: *inspected-test retrospective* (later recordings of people the model was trained on, test segment already seen), *participant-held-out internal* (people held out entirely, but already inspected in earlier experiments), *external cohort*, *re-analysis* (saved predictions re-used), *synthetic* and *software test*. None of them is clinical validation.

**12 of 21 claims match their artifacts; 0 mismatch; 0 artifact(s) missing on this installation; 0 author-reported only; 0 awaiting README wording.**

